name 'designing-reliable-apps-postassessment-q9_2025'

question 'A developer fetches an array of 8 book objects and writes JavaScript that loops through the array and creates a <div> for each book. Before the fetch runs, how many book <div> elements exist in the HTML file?'

right 'Zero — the book divs are generated dynamically by JavaScript, not written in the HTML file'
wrong 'Eight — the HTML file must contain placeholder divs that JavaScript fills with content'
wrong 'One — the HTML file contains a single template div that JavaScript copies for each book'
wrong 'It depends on how many books were returned by the API on the previous page load'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 6
MARKDOWN
